{"item_id":"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/how-to-properly-wash-and-maintain-your-rucksack-a-complete","version_id":"0fa57c5da5898330cf3c4113db7d48612d0ae695287bade43de32ee3992f5f4a","decision":"defer","reason":"Under Relevance, pack maintenance transfers to repeated muddy, sweaty loaded carries, but Freshness and novelty and Making the decision favor deferral because this recent guide compiles existing manufacturer care instructions without new testing, field experience, or newly reported problems. Under Credibility and Commercial incentives, those instructions support attributed care guidance rather than independent durability findings; the publisher earns affiliate commissions, has received GORUCK review units, and publishes at unusually high volume.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/how-to-start-a-ruck-club","version_id":"bdd20224acc1ebef791a53609336021c99786335082d3c36d138d8c884c7e081","decision":"reject","reason":"Under Relevance and Making the decision, this is a community-organizing and training-session guide, with only incidental pack suggestions and no substantive evidence about gear performance under Mammoth conditions. Commercial incentives include affiliate commissions, previously supplied GORUCK review units, and promotion of the publisher's own club directory.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/black-diamond-distance-15-backpack-review","version_id":"72a94336aee944d2865b19aa22833a0909ed2257f9513c0bece6e9d6948f3840","decision":"accept","reason":"Under Relevance, Credibility, and Freshness and novelty, several months of newly reported alpine testing provide citable observations about abrasion resistance, pocket access, and bounce and discomfort with heavy water loads, supporting Pieces 01, 02, and 03. Commercial incentives and Uncertainty require noting affiliate commissions and attributing results to this reviewer; Suitability and official requirements limits extrapolation from a 15-liter running pack to multi-day Mammoth loads and leaves required status unspecified.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/camping-outdoor-blankets","version_id":"4cee453e4397415960c54f3e35b7b1cac2b511cd28774f12f81d4d6a7c5f4a","decision":"accept","reason":"Under Relevance, Credibility, and Freshness and novelty, the updated field experience and described half-liter leakage tests provide citable sleep-system evidence, including the Original Puffy's inadequate warmth in the 40s and the Backcountry blanket's reported cold-weather use, supporting Pieces 01, 02, and 03. Commercial incentives and Uncertainty require disclosing affiliate commissions, treating this as one publisher's evidence, and keeping Rumpl's precise warmth and packability claims unverified; Suitability and official requirements permits practical discussion without asserting an official requirement or a validated sleeping-bag replacement.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://soldiersystems.net/2026/10/15/army-hosts-international-signing-ceremony-for-uas-and-counter-uas-marketplaces-at-ausa-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=army-hosts-international-signing-ceremony-for-uas-and-counter-uas-marketplaces-at-ausa-2026","version_id":"111fd9afec5b36a2ce1f292d4e3459830d2a9d12a45082702214c53d576512d6","decision":"reject","reason":"Under Relevance and Making the decision, this Army Public Affairs release concerns international drone procurement platforms rather than eligible competitor gear or Mammoth carry decisions. Under Commercial incentives, the commercial publisher is reproducing institutional procurement messaging, not independent gear testing.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://soldiersystems.net/2026/10/14/arkeus-warden-hyperspectral-optical-radar-enters-australian-army-service/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=arkeus-warden-hyperspectral-optical-radar-enters-australian-army-service","version_id":"2e678b344ac42150b9d9469811990eb6350d1930c4c6f9047b0b713b9c02b3f6","decision":"reject","reason":"Under Relevance and Making the decision, Warden is an aircraft-mounted military surveillance payload, outside the competitor spotting and measuring gear covered by the policy and unconnected to Mammoth carry decisions. Commercial incentives and Credibility identify its superiority and degraded-condition performance claims as manufacturer and integration-partner messaging without independently described tests.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://soldiersystems.net/2026/10/14/introducing-flymotion-airmesh/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=introducing-flymotion-airmesh","version_id":"a7bf8f597d01174372efa7a0518cff1d86d74b98da2368e4ab593479017e831c","decision":"reject","reason":"Under Relevance and Making the decision, this promotional announcement covers a drone-mounted communications relay outside the eligible gear categories, with no supported Mammoth application. Commercial incentives and Unsupported claims identify manufacturer assertions about range, bandwidth, and resilience without substantive test evidence.","piece_ids":[]}
